                <pb facs="0607" n="525" xml:id="pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2680.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 30, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1176.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that Gen.
                    Bernardo Reyes, who voluntarily surrendered to a small detachment of Federal
                    rurales at Ciudad Linares early on Christmas morning, was brought to this city
                    on the 28th instant by a small detachment of soldiers and was immediately taken
                    to the Santiago prison, where he will be confined until arrangements are made
                    for his trial.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
